      "noisiest_factor": "dSC",
      "prose": "Net carries forward at <strong>r &asymp; 0.89</strong> against a five-year-trailing target (the table above, n&nbsp;=&nbsp;17,204) &mdash; but that is inflated by <em>window overlap</em>: the target board shares most of today's data. Scored over the same 2021\u20132025 transition blocks &mdash; the very same <strong>2,157</strong> player-seasons on both sides &mdash; the same board reaches <strong>r = 0.893</strong> against that overlapping target but only <strong>0.498</strong> against a genuinely <strong>non-overlapping single-season</strong> target &mdash; an overlap inflation of <strong>0.395</strong>, not skill. Shooting efficiency (oTS &asymp; 0.49) and forcing turnovers (dTOV &asymp; 0.49) carry forward best; defensive second-chance (dSC &asymp; 0.27) is the noisiest.",
      "_note": "gap = retro_net_report.json `inflation`: row-matched, so both legs are the SAME 2157 rows (n_fiveyr == n_single_season, enforced by _gate_overlap_identity). NOT next_season.net.corr - single_season_pooled_r: those are different panels (n=17204 vs n=2157) and subtracting them is a cross-sample error."
    },
